=====================

   S~S  Release notes version 260304: publish v1.0a to the public consumer

------------------------------------------

    "template document files" is a collection of documents about the format and content
    of the human metadata files, as defined by the culture of the SimpleSal organization.

    In the future, when publishing a SimpleSal App, the task list might include:

        copy the template files into the instance directory containing the managed object

        edit the copied versions as recommended by the template files

        add the edited files to the repository in the repo root

------------------------------------------

=====================

   S~S  Release notes version 260201: update template copyright message within metadata files

------------------------------------------

    The year of copyright assertion within a template document is the projected year of publishment.

------------------------------------------

=====================

   S~S  Release notes version 260105: template-docs repository activity: create the repository

------------------------------------------

    Instantiate the repository version control database from file system version control database.

    This collection of human metadata files were instantiated into the rr\template-docs directory.
    All of the files except LICENSE were created from scratch by TSC LLC for SimpleSal repos.

        rr\README                    an introduction, a window, a sales pitch about the content
        rr\FUTURES                   a hallucination, a dream, customer demand about the content
        rr\RELEASE                   instantaneous description of a release of content at Time X
        rr\CHANGELOG                 cumulative RELEASE descrptions at Time X, Y, Z

        rr\LICENSE                   as emitted by GitHub license Application: GPL 3.0 selected
        rr\LICENSE-TSC-LLC           an interpretation of what TSC LLC wants the license to be
        rr\COPYING                   a clear statement that copying and using needs no license

        rr\master-format-example     TSC LLC view of a format

